course: dictionary
lesson: 10423
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning the writer chose. «The troll lived under the old stone bridge.» Caves, mountains and bridges are clues that this is a creature from a fairy tale.
explain: «He posts a cruel message to upset strangers every day.» Posts and messages are clues that this troll is a person online. A troll is someone who posts nasty or silly messages on purpose to upset people.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «A troll farm is an office of people paid to post under fake names.» Does «a fake name office» make sense? Yes, so the online meaning fits here.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Troll» (fairy tale) means a big, ugly, often stupid creature that lives in caves, mountains or under bridges.
fact: «Troll» (internet) means a person who posts nasty or silly messages online on purpose to upset people or start arguments.
fact: «Troll» as a verb can mean to post such messages, or to fish by pulling a baited line slowly behind a boat.
fact: Online safety tip: don't feed the trolls. Do not reply, block and report, and tell an adult.
exercise: «The troll lived under the old stone bridge and scared the goats.» What is a troll in this sentence? | A type of fish | A goat herder | *A big, ugly creature from a fairy tale | A kind helper who mends bridges
exercise: Someone posts a cruel message online just to upset a stranger. What is this person called? | A fairy-tale giant | *An internet troll | A teacher | A fisherman
exercise: Mum says, «Don't feed the trolls, just block and report.» What should you do? | Post it again to get even | Reply with a rude message | Share the message with all your friends | *Do not reply, block and report, and tell an adult
test: «A troll farm is an office of people paid to post under fake names.» What are the people in a troll farm paid to do? | Tell fairy tales | *Post under fake names | Build bridges | Catch fish
test: Dad will troll for fish on the lake this morning. What does troll mean here? | *Pull a baited line slowly behind a boat | Post nasty messages | Frighten the goats | Hide under a bridge
exam: Read: «The troll posted three cruel comments before lunch.» What does troll mean here? | To fish with a baited line | A big, stupid giant in a fairy tale | A creature in a cave | *A person who posts nasty messages online on purpose
